<title>BELGIUM: Farm ministers discuss tobacco report.</title>
<headline>Farm ministers discuss tobacco report.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union farm ministers on Monday discussed a tobacco report urging that EU subsidies should be aimed at improving quality and encouraging farmers to stop production, EU officials said.</p>
<p>Spain, Greece, Italy and Portugal criticised the report though they said it was a basis for discussion.</p>
<p>The four producer countries criticised the idea of linking subsidies to market prices, saying that quality depended on other factors.</p>
<p>They also opposed a move to reduce national production quotas when farmers retire or switch to other activities.</p>
<p>After the European Parliament has given an opinion on the report (COM 96/554), the Commission will draft a proposal for reforms.</p>
</text>
